summary:
  The relay re-arm that keeps a live listener's music going fires over a PARK
  too, so a paused Ogg or FLAC station starts itself when its capture writer
  reaches the window cap.

history:
  The writer carries ffmpeg's -t <window>, so it exits by itself after an hour.
  For a live relay listener that exit is a re-arm; the player coasts while a
  fresh tap comes up. The engine's own `shifted` turns true only on a RESUME,
  so a parked relay looked exactly like a playing one from in there — and the
  park lives on the app side, where nothing was asked. The UP ack then reached
  tsPlayRelay, which clears _tsPaused and plays. Pause before lunch, music an
  hour later with nobody in the room. Found 2026-09-14, issue #13's shape from
  a wall clock alone.

target:
  package/contents/ui/TimeshiftEngine.qml

find:
              if (relay && !shifted && !app._tsPaused

replace:
              if (relay && !shifted

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_timeshiftengine.qml::test_a_parked_relay_is_not_woken_by_its_own_window_cap.
  Line-neutral.
